## 4. High-Level Architecture

Git is the single source of truth. Engineers merge PRs that update Helm values (image digests) and platform manifests. GitHub Actions authenticates to GCP via Workload Identity Federation, builds or mirrors images, scans with Trivy, signs with cosign, and pushes to Artifact Registry. Argo CD watches the repo and syncs desired state to a **single private regional GKE cluster**. Platform components (Kyverno, ESO, NetworkPolicy) enforce security at admission and runtime. Online Boutique runs in the `boutique` namespace; Argo CD in `argocd`; observability stack in `monitoring`.

North-south traffic enters through a Google Cloud external HTTP(S) load balancer with a static IP, Google-managed TLS certificates, and Cloud Armor WAF rules. OpenTelemetry collectors receive app telemetry and export to Cloud Trace and Managed Prometheus; Grafana dashboards visualize service health. Cloud Monitoring hosts SLOs, uptime checks, and burn-rate alert policies that notify PagerDuty with links to runbooks in `docs/sre/runbooks/`.

