## 8. Network Flow

### VPC Layout

```
VPC (custom mode)
├── Subnet: gke-nodes (private primary IPs for nodes)
├── Subnet: gke-pods (secondary range — alias IP)
├── Subnet: gke-services (secondary range — ClusterIP)
├── Cloud Router + Cloud NAT (private node egress to internet)
├── Firewall: allow health checks, deny broad ingress to nodes
└── Private Google Access enabled (GCP API reachability)
```

### GKE Networking

- **Private cluster:** Node IPs not publicly routable
- **Authorized networks** or IAP for control plane access (admin kubectl)
- **Ingress:** GCE Ingress controller provisions external HTTP(S) LB
- **Static global IP** reserved in Terraform; bound to Ingress annotations

### NetworkPolicy Model (default-deny)

| Namespace | Ingress allowed from | Egress allowed to |
|-----------|---------------------|-------------------|
| `boutique` | Ingress controller, same-namespace services | DNS, deps per service matrix, OTel collector |
| `argocd` | Ingress (argocd host), Git (egress) | GKE API, repo, managed certs |
| `monitoring` | All namespaces (scrape) | Managed Prometheus endpoint, Grafana deps |
| `kyverno` | Kubernetes API | Webhook targets |
| `external-secrets` | Kubernetes API | Secret Manager API (private Google access) |

Labels on pods (e.g. `network-policy/boutique: "true"`) required by Kyverno policy #4.

