## 9. Security Boundaries

| Boundary | Mechanism | Notes |
|----------|-----------|-------|
| **CI → GCP** | WIF (OIDC trust GitHub repo/ref) | Short-lived tokens; scoped SA per workflow |
| **Pod → GCP APIs** | Workload Identity | ESO SA binds to K8s SA in `external-secrets` |
| **Image trust** | cosign + Binary Authorization | Unsigned/unattested images rejected at deploy |
| **Admission** | Kyverno | Blocks `:latest`, missing probes, plain Secrets |
| **Runtime network** | NetworkPolicy | Default-deny; explicit service graph |
| **Edge** | Cloud Armor | OWASP CRS baseline; geo/rate rules as needed |
| **Secrets** | Secret Manager + ESO | No secrets in Git; gitleaks in pre-commit |
| **Audit** | Cloud Audit Logs | Admin activity, data access, policy denials |
| **TLS** | Google-managed certs | Auto-renewal on Ingress |
| **RBAC** | K8s RBAC + GCP IAM | Least privilege for human and automation SAs |

**Trust zones:**

```
Untrusted (Internet)
  → Cloud Armor + TLS (edge trust)
  → Ingress (cluster edge)
  → boutique namespace (app trust — NetworkPolicy segmented)
  → Platform namespaces (elevated — restricted RBAC)
  → GCP control plane APIs (Workload Identity scoped)
```

