## 14. Cost Considerations

- **Single cluster** avoids duplicate control-plane and baseline platform costs vs multi-cluster
- **Private nodes + NAT** incur NAT gateway egress charges — acceptable for reference scale
- **Managed Prometheus + Cloud Monitoring** — tune retention; avoid high-cardinality labels
- **Static IP + LB** — fixed monthly cost while cluster exists
- **Always-on node pool** — use autoscaling min=1 or small pool; tear down when not in use
- **GKE Backup storage** — GCS costs for Redis backups; schedule aligned to RPO needs

---

## 15. Tradeoffs

| Decision | Chosen | Alternative rejected | Rationale |
|----------|--------|---------------------|-----------|
| **One cluster** | Namespace isolation | Multi-project/cluster per env | Cost, simplicity, portfolio scope; patterns still transferable |
| **Manual Argo sync** | Operator approves sync | Auto-sync | Prevents surprise deploys; teaches production promotion discipline |
| **No service mesh** | NetworkPolicy + Ingress | Istio/Linkerd | Mesh adds ops burden; not needed for Boutique's service graph |
| **Upstream images** | Mirror + digest pin | Fork/custom code | Focus on platform/SRE depth, not app dev |
| **GCE Ingress** | Native GCP LB + Armor | nginx-only ingress | Integrated TLS, Armor, static IP on GCP |
| **WIF** | OIDC federation | Downloaded SA keys | Security baseline; no key rotation burden |
| **ESO-only secrets** | Secret Manager via ESO | Sealed Secrets / plain K8s Secrets | Native GCP integration; audit trail in Cloud Audit Logs |

